## GitHub Workflow

All project work will be tracked through GitHub Issues and the GitHub Projects board.

For each user story or task:

1. Create or assign a GitHub Issue.
2. Create a separate branch for the issue.
3. Make and commit changes on that branch.
4. Push the branch to GitHub.
5. Open a pull request into `main`.
6. Have the other team member review the pull request.
7. Merge the pull request after approval.

Project changes will not be pushed directly to `main`.